1
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Look with your heart and truly see

2
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:36,000
The truth is waiting not far away

3
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:39,000
Hey you good or bad, truth and lies

4
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Can't escape the smog inside your soul

5
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:45,000
Bring with you all of your courage

6
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:48,000
And maybe you will save this world

7
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:51,000
Mojo Mojo Mojo Spy

8
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Mojo Mojo Mojo Spy

9
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:57,000
Mojo Mojo Mojo Spy

10
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:13,000
Right into the trap

11
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:29,700
Aw, you poor little thing

12
00:01:29,700 --> 00:01:32,680
If it weren't for removing those

13
00:01:32,680 --> 00:01:35,159
clowns blocking the great Illumin-Eye's plan

14
00:01:35,159 --> 00:01:39,200
you wouldn't have suffered like this

15
00:01:39,200 --> 00:01:41,920
But now

16
00:01:41,920 --> 00:01:43,920
the clown has taken the bait

17
00:01:43,920 --> 00:01:46,200
so you can go back to normal

18
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:00,879
Come on

19
00:02:20,879 --> 00:02:24,420
Looks like the clown's envy time is over

20
00:02:36,400 --> 00:02:38,000
The target's gone

21
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:42,720
Let's keep searching along the lakeside

22
00:02:42,720 --> 00:02:44,820
Maybe we'll find some traces

23
00:02:44,820 --> 00:02:48,020
The suspect's completely out of our sensor range

24
00:02:48,780 --> 00:02:51,220
The thermal scan can't be wrong

25
00:02:51,220 --> 00:02:54,060
Tsk, how is that possible?

26
00:02:54,060 --> 00:02:56,259
Don't tell me he simply vanished into thin air!

27
00:02:56,259 --> 00:02:59,219
That's because your captain stalled for time,

28
00:02:59,219 --> 00:03:02,080
giving the suspect a chance to escape.

29
00:03:02,080 --> 00:03:05,460
You—you're talking nonsense!

30
00:03:05,460 --> 00:03:07,640
Captain Han put your safety first in everything,

31
00:03:07,640 --> 00:03:09,000
yet you still slander him!

32
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:10,640
This isn't the time to quarrel.

33
00:03:10,640 --> 00:03:12,680
Since the suspect has already vanished,

34
00:03:12,680 --> 00:03:16,840
we might as well go back to base and join up with Captain Han.

35
00:03:16,840 --> 00:03:18,520
Then we can think this through properly.

36
00:03:18,520 --> 00:03:20,640
There's nothing else to do now.

37
00:03:20,640 --> 00:03:22,659
It's getting dark fast.

38
00:03:22,659 --> 00:03:24,500
In woods this big, once night falls,

39
00:03:24,500 --> 00:03:26,699
there's no telling what might come crawling out.

40
00:03:26,699 --> 00:03:28,180
You people who can't make up your minds—

41
00:03:28,180 --> 00:03:30,800
you'll just let the suspect escape again!

42
00:03:30,800 --> 00:03:32,379
You—!

43
00:03:32,379 --> 00:03:37,460
Doctor, are you all right?

44
00:03:37,460 --> 00:03:42,639
I must have twisted my ankle running too fast.

45
00:03:42,639 --> 00:03:45,139
I'm such a fool.

46
00:03:45,139 --> 00:03:48,960
Doctor, you really didn't have to come along.

47
00:03:48,960 --> 00:03:51,519
It's all my fault—I'm useless.

48
00:03:52,659 --> 00:03:55,180
I lured them to the lakeside as agreed,

49
00:03:55,180 --> 00:03:56,840
but Dorothy is nowhere to be seen.

50
00:03:56,840 --> 00:03:59,759
If I keep up this act much longer, I'm afraid I'll blow my cover.

51
00:03:59,759 --> 00:04:02,919
Dorothy, where on earth are you?

52
00:04:02,919 --> 00:04:06,019
Doctor, you don't have to blame yourself so much.

53
00:04:06,019 --> 00:04:09,259
You only came because you wanted to talk Storm out of it face-to-face.

54
00:04:09,259 --> 00:04:12,620
Since Storm's gone now,

55
00:04:12,620 --> 00:04:14,919
let's just rest here a bit

56
00:04:14,919 --> 00:04:16,720
before heading back to meet Officer Han.

57
00:04:16,720 --> 00:04:19,300
How boring.

58
00:04:19,300 --> 00:04:20,939
What did you say?

59
00:04:20,939 --> 00:04:24,680
Hey, Inspector Sima! Inspector Sima, do you read me?

60
00:04:24,680 --> 00:04:29,219
I read you—come in, come in, Inspector Sima!

61
00:04:29,219 --> 00:04:35,319
Captain Han, this is Sima. The signal here is really terrible.

62
00:04:35,319 --> 00:04:39,500
Inspector Sima, you all must be careful with Dr. Breeze—he's Storm in disguise!

63
00:04:39,500 --> 00:04:45,839
Hey, what's wrong with Dr. Breeze? He's perfectly safe. I can't hear you—disguised as what?

64
00:04:45,840 --> 00:04:53,480
Hey, Inspector Sima! Inspector Sima, can you hear me? Inspector Sima? Hey—hey, are you there? Hey!

65
00:04:53,480 --> 00:05:03,840
Dr. Breeze, are you out of your mind? Put the gun down!

66
00:05:09,800 --> 00:05:10,199
Keep the "Doctor" title for my dear big brother.

67
00:05:10,319 --> 00:05:12,099
As for me,

68
00:05:12,099 --> 00:05:14,680
I prefer to be called—

69
00:05:14,680 --> 00:05:15,819
Hunter Storm!

70
00:05:15,819 --> 00:05:18,279
So you're Storm after all!

71
00:05:18,279 --> 00:05:21,379
I never thought my true identity...

72
00:05:21,379 --> 00:05:22,899
would be exposed this quickly.

73
00:05:22,899 --> 00:05:24,399
But just as planned,

74
00:05:24,399 --> 00:05:26,139
I've managed to lure you all here.

75
00:05:26,139 --> 00:05:28,839
That's quite an achievement.

76
00:05:28,839 --> 00:05:31,399
What plan?

77
00:05:31,399 --> 00:05:33,579
And the real Dr. Breeze—

78
00:05:33,579 --> 00:05:34,860
what exactly did you do to him?

79
00:05:34,860 --> 00:05:38,360
Great detectives.

80
00:05:38,360 --> 00:05:40,039
The two questions you asked—

81
00:05:40,040 --> 00:05:42,120
well, that's a long story.

82
00:05:42,120 --> 00:05:43,780
Alright,

83
00:05:43,780 --> 00:05:46,180
let me start with my dear brother.

84
00:05:46,180 --> 00:05:48,580
I snuck into the lab and knocked him out.

85
00:05:48,580 --> 00:05:52,700
Then I hid him in a petri dish.

86
00:05:52,700 --> 00:05:55,780
To fool you all,

87
00:05:55,780 --> 00:05:58,040
I had to smash my head against the wall

88
00:05:58,040 --> 00:05:59,900
and make myself bleed.

89
00:05:59,900 --> 00:06:03,540
Who'd have thought you famous detectives

90
00:06:03,540 --> 00:06:05,660
would be fooled so easily by me?

91
00:06:05,660 --> 00:06:08,099
Dr. Breeze is your own brother.

92
00:06:08,199 --> 00:06:10,579
And he's been worried about you all along.

93
00:06:10,579 --> 00:06:12,420
You're worse than a beast—

94
00:06:12,420 --> 00:06:14,079
laying a hand on your own brother!

95
00:06:14,079 --> 00:06:16,699
Own brother? Worried?

96
00:06:16,699 --> 00:06:20,439
Don't make me laugh.

97
00:06:20,439 --> 00:06:22,759
Ever since I was a kid,

98
00:06:22,759 --> 00:06:24,120
all the good things

99
00:06:24,120 --> 00:06:25,740
were hogged by this dear brother.

100
00:06:25,740 --> 00:06:27,519
In my parents' eyes—

101
00:06:27,519 --> 00:06:29,379
He was always the best.

102
00:06:29,379 --> 00:06:31,620
No matter how hard I tried, I could never match him.

103
00:06:31,620 --> 00:06:33,620
I was invisible to my parents.

104
00:06:33,620 --> 00:06:34,939
All I could do was spend my entire life

105
00:06:34,939 --> 00:06:36,279
in his shadow.

106
00:06:36,279 --> 00:06:37,899
After we grew up,

107
00:06:37,900 --> 00:06:39,640
he was still sailing smoothly,

108
00:06:39,640 --> 00:06:41,540
while I kept hitting walls left and right.

109
00:06:41,540 --> 00:06:43,380
When I ran into trouble,

110
00:06:43,380 --> 00:06:46,320
how I wished my big brother would come help me.

111
00:06:46,320 --> 00:06:49,080
But all he cared about was studying those awful animals.

112
00:06:49,080 --> 00:06:51,120
He never once came to me.

113
00:06:51,120 --> 00:06:53,880
His mind had room for nothing but his research.

114
00:06:53,880 --> 00:06:57,440
In the end, I could only make a living by poaching.

115
00:06:57,440 --> 00:06:59,680
This hatred I had for my so-called brother,

116
00:06:59,680 --> 00:07:02,040
I poured it all onto the little animals he loved.

117
00:07:02,040 --> 00:07:05,299
If not for that,

118
00:07:05,379 --> 00:07:08,779
I wouldn't have ended up as a slave of the Illumin-Eye.

119
00:07:08,779 --> 00:07:12,680
Hmph. So it's them after all.

120
00:07:12,680 --> 00:07:15,699
What exactly are you going to do with us?

121
00:07:15,699 --> 00:07:19,420
My only job was to lure you here.

122
00:07:19,420 --> 00:07:21,000
What happens next,

123
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:23,199
you'll have to ask my partner.

124
00:07:23,199 --> 00:07:25,219
Dorothy!

125
00:07:25,219 --> 00:07:26,819
Where are you?

126
00:07:26,819 --> 00:07:28,600
I've already succeeded.

127
00:07:45,399 --> 00:07:46,040
So they were underwater.

128
00:07:46,040 --> 00:07:48,060
No wonder the thermal sensors

129
00:07:48,060 --> 00:07:48,879
couldn't find them.

130
00:07:48,879 --> 00:07:50,579
Dorothy.

131
00:07:50,579 --> 00:07:52,100
As promised,

132
00:07:52,100 --> 00:07:53,199
I've lured them here.

133
00:07:53,199 --> 00:07:55,560
My score with your organization

134
00:07:55,560 --> 00:07:56,779
is settled once and for all.

135
00:07:56,779 --> 00:07:58,439
From now on, we—

136
00:08:11,399 --> 00:08:12,920
Those who know our organization's secrets

137
00:08:12,920 --> 00:08:14,319
don't just get to walk away.

138
00:08:14,319 --> 00:08:17,740
If you don't want to end up

139
00:08:17,740 --> 00:08:19,279
like this talkative one,

140
00:08:19,279 --> 00:08:21,740
stay right where you are.

141
00:08:21,740 --> 00:08:22,639
Don't move.

142
00:08:22,639 --> 00:08:25,100
Especially you,

143
00:08:25,100 --> 00:08:27,519
my dear little puppet.

144
00:08:27,520 --> 00:08:35,920
So The Illumin-Eye is stirring up trouble again.

145
00:08:35,920 --> 00:08:39,480
But why would you kill your own accomplice?

146
00:08:39,480 --> 00:08:42,920
Mr. Chen,

147
00:08:42,920 --> 00:08:46,160
please don't casually use that ugly word "kill."

148
00:08:46,160 --> 00:08:48,720
He isn't dead.

149
00:08:48,720 --> 00:08:53,540
He's merely become crystal-clear amber.

150
00:08:57,519 --> 00:09:02,740
Don't you think that ugly man, once adorned with amber,

151
00:09:02,740 --> 00:09:05,779
Are you even more beautiful and charming now?

152
00:09:05,779 --> 00:09:08,500
He must have been kicked in the head by a donkey.

153
00:09:08,500 --> 00:09:11,519
Thanks to this ugly, big-mouthed fool,

154
00:09:11,519 --> 00:09:14,139
I finally got the chance to catch all of you—

155
00:09:14,139 --> 00:09:16,659
maggots obstructing the Illumin-Eye's great revival!

156
00:09:16,659 --> 00:09:19,819
Though a few maggots are still missing,

157
00:09:19,819 --> 00:09:21,579
and that does disappoint me.

158
00:09:21,579 --> 00:09:24,720
But I'm sure it won't be long

159
00:09:24,720 --> 00:09:27,980
before I have them all rounded up.

160
00:09:27,980 --> 00:09:30,879
So, for what comes next,

161
00:09:30,879 --> 00:09:34,279
let me help you shed those hideous flesh sacks

162
00:09:34,279 --> 00:09:37,620
and turn into gorgeous amber.

163
00:10:24,720 --> 00:10:25,799
I will turn you into the most beautiful work of art.

164
00:10:49,759 --> 00:10:50,460
Stop.

165
00:10:50,460 --> 00:10:51,720
You puppet.

166
00:10:51,720 --> 00:10:53,960
You have no right to choose.

167
00:10:53,960 --> 00:10:55,960
Bye-bye.